From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:25:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: restart radar detection after a full
 reset

mt7915_dfs_init_radar_detector() only talks to the firmware when the
DFS state changes, and phy->dfs_state is only reset when the channel or
width changes or the regulatory domain is updated. After a full chip
reset the firmware is reloaded without a running radar detector, but
mac80211 restores the same channel, so the state is unchanged and
RDD_START/CAC_END are never sent again: radar detection stays off on
the operating DFS channel until the channel changes.

Reset the DFS state of both bands during the full reset, as the
regulatory notifier already does, so the detector is set up again when
the channel is restored.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index ff69cf8e..dcd44c05 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1459,6 +1459,11 @@ mt7915_mac_full_reset(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 	if (phy2)
 		phy2->omac_mask = 0;
 
+	/* the restarted firmware has no radar detector running */
+	dev->mphy.dfs_state = MT_DFS_STATE_UNKNOWN;
+	if (ext_phy)
+		ext_phy->dfs_state = MT_DFS_STATE_UNKNOWN;
+
 	mt76_reset_device(&dev->mt76);
 
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->sta_rc_list);
